WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.169 --> 00:00:01.002
(crowd cheers)

00:00:01.002 --> 00:00:03.510
- We had a big day today

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.340
and don't let those cheaters

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.315
and crooks think anything different.

00:00:07.315 --> 00:00:08.148
(crowd cheers)

00:00:08.148 --> 00:00:09.150
- [Narrator] Republican candidates

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.940
who have echoed former President
Donald Trump's false claims

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.980
that the 2020 was fraudulent

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.440
lost some crucial races this election.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.273
- That's right.

00:00:17.273 --> 00:00:18.780
- [Narrator] While others
have not yet been called

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.970
by the Associated Press.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.130
Election skeptic candidates
were on the ballot

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.080
for governor and secretary of state

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.270
across the country on Tuesday.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.070
But in a few key swing states,

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.260
these offices could have the most impact

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.680
on the 2024 General Election and beyond.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.780
That's because governors
and secretaries of state

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.200
have considerable authority
over election administration

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.910
and in 2020, Nevada, Arizona,
Michigan, and Pennsylvania

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.910
were all decided by thin vote margin.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.730
Here's a breakdown of how
election skeptic candidates fared

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.800
in each of those states.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.398
- This is a movement.

00:00:54.398 --> 00:00:56.981
(gentle music)

00:00:58.296 --> 00:00:59.220
- [Narrator] In Pennsylvania,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.350
Republican Doug Mastriano was defeated

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.380
in his race for governor
by Democrat Josh Shapiro,

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.630
according to the Associated Press.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:09.480
As a state senator, Mastriano
introduced legislation

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.730
to ignore the 2020 election result

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:14.550
and directly appoint
electors pledged to Trump,

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.450
despite the fact

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.880
that there was no evidence
of widespread fraud.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.610
- It's something very near and
dear to both of our hearts.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.590
We're gonna fight like
hell for voting integrity

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.015
and we're gonna start with voter ID.

00:01:24.015 --> 00:01:24.848
(crowd cheers)

00:01:24.848 --> 00:01:25.681
- [Narrator] In Pennsylvania,

00:01:25.681 --> 00:01:27.960
the governor directly appoints
the secretary of state

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.700
and other election officials

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.758
and therefore can significantly
influence election policy.

00:01:33.758 --> 00:01:36.258
(tense music)

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.900
- Why do we have a secretary of state

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.730
that wants to go around the rules?

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.650
- [Narrator] In Michigan,
Republican Tudor Dixon

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.330
was defeated in her race for governor

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.600
by incumbent Gretchen
Whitmer, according to the AP.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.120
During her campaign, Dixon
repeated false claims

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.190
that the 2020 election result in Michigan

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:55.440
was altered by widespread fraud.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.710
If elected, she had pledged
to enact strict voter ID laws,

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:02.220
ban ballot drop boxes, and
launch retroactive investigations

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.976
into the 2020 election.

00:02:03.976 --> 00:02:05.790
- We're insurrectionists, we're traitors,

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:08.040
big lie proponents for asking questions.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.720
- [Narrator] And
Republican Kristina Karamo

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.640
lost her race for secretary of state

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.310
against the Democrat
incumbent Jocelyn Benson,

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.140
according to the AP.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.230
Karamo ran on the America First
slate of election skeptics

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.783
and has repeated false
claims of election fraud.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.300
The Michigan secretary of state

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.040
does not have the centralized authority

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.690
over election certification

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.240
that many other secretaries of state have,

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.080
but he or she can issue directives
to local election offices

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.730
and trigger audits,

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.463
as allies of President Trump did in 2020.

00:02:39.448 --> 00:02:43.080
(bright tonal music)

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.336
- Is this the greatest
president we're ever known?

00:02:45.336 --> 00:02:46.740
(crowd cheers)

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:47.610
- [Narrator] In Arizona,

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.680
the governor's race has
still not been called

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.660
between former TV anchor Kari Lake

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:54.120
and Democrat Katie Hobbs.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.830
Lake was among the most visible

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.680
and vocal skeptics of the 2020 election.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.240
She had aligned herself with Trump,

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.960
who made Arizona a focal point
of his false election claims.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.450
- I'd actually like to ask
everybody on this stage

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.570
if they would agree we had
a corrupt, stolen election.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.070
Raise your hand.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:13.260
- [Narrator] Official
investigations, court cases,

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.260
and election audits have not
substantiated allegations

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.360
of widespread fraud.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.670
In Arizona, the governor
and secretary of state

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.100
can enact sweeping changes to elections,

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.780
especially if their party controls

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.730
the state legislature too.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:27.720
In her campaign,

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.450
Lake didn't specify all of
the changes she would make,

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.730
but she signaled
opposition to early voting

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:33.960
and mail-in ballots.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.670
- Our Constitution says Election Day,

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.460
it doesn't say election
season, election month.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.470
- [Narrator] The race for
Arizona secretary of state

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:43.530
has also not been called
between Republican Mark Finchem

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.230
and Democrat Adrian Fontes.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.060
In Arizona, the secretary of state

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.730
is in charge of certifying elections.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.140
As a state representative,

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.670
Finchem introduced legislation

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.040
to decertify the 2020 election,

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.560
and during his campaign
for secretary of state,

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.100
he often repeated unfounded
claims of widespread fraud.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.290
- There are certain counties
that should've been set aside

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.790
as irredeemably compromised.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.740
Maricopa County was one of them.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.450
- [Narrator] In Arizona,
the secretary of state

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.390
has broad powers over
election administration.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.520
Previously, Finchem had expressed a desire

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:18.576
to decertify many of
Arizona's election machines.

00:04:18.576 --> 00:04:21.930
(serious tonal music)

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:23.100
- Your name, sir?

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.830
- Jim Marchant from Las Vegas, Nevada.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.800
We are here to recommend
that you vote today

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.390
to dispose of your electronic
voting and tabulation machines

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:37.230
and do not use them in any
elections going forward.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.030
- [Narrator] The race for
Nevada secretary of state

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:42.000
has still not been called
between Republican Jim Marchant

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.820
and his Democratic
opponent, Cisco Aguilar.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:48.120
Marchant has made false claims
about the 2020 election.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.680
- We have something in common.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.680
President Trump and I
lost an election in 2020

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.518
because of a rigged election.

00:04:54.518 --> 00:04:55.351
- [Crowd] Yeah!

00:04:55.351 --> 00:04:56.370
- [Narrator] Ahead of the midterms,

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.380
Marchant led an organized campaign

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.210
to support election skeptic candidates

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.850
for secretary of state nationwide.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:07.800
- Last year, I established a
MAGA America First coalition

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.860
of secretary of state
candidates around the country.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.410
- [Narrator] Marchant's group,
the America First slate,

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.080
included a dozen candidates
for secretary of state

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.270
and supported the gubernatorial campaigns

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:21.879
of Kari Lake in Arizona and
Doug Mastriano in Pennsylvania.

00:05:21.879 --> 00:05:23.430
(crowd cheers)
(crowd applauds)

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:24.263
- Oh yeah.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.910
- [Narrator] Election skeptic candidates

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.950
lost some important bids to take the reins

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:31.170
of election administration
in swing states,

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.270
while others remain uncalled.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:36.420
Changes to election processes
in any one of these states

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:39.775
could be the factor that tips
a close election in 2024.

00:05:39.775 --> 00:05:42.775
(tense tonal music)

